# What the Docker daemon sees inside an already-uploaded build context.
#
# Not redundant with .gcloudignore -- the two govern different stages. That
# file decides what leaves this machine; this one decides what the daemon can
# see, and keeps a future local `docker build` behaving like a Cloud Build.
# The Dockerfile COPYs explicit paths rather than `COPY . .`, so this is
# defence-in-depth. Do not delete either one as a duplicate of the other.

.venv/
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# The unstripped 978 MB checkpoint. scripts/strip_checkpoint.py produces the
# weights-only file below, which is what the image actually needs.
checkpoints/*
!checkpoints/ckpt_5000.weights.pt

# Copyrighted corpus; the derived tokenizer is what ships.
data/book.pdf
data/book.txt

# Training and retraining only -- not part of the served surface. infer.py is
# excluded deliberately: it imports transformers, which is in no requirements
# file, so shipping it would put a guaranteed-broken module in the image.
train.py
train_tokenizer.py
extract_text.py
test_tokenizer.py
infer.py
tests/
inference/
requirements-dev.txt
README.md

.gcloudignore
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
